---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import AffiliateLink from "../../components/AffiliateLink.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Mario Kart World — Switch 2 Buying Guide"
  description="Is Mario Kart World worth it on Switch 2? Editions, Knockout Tour, and where to buy the digital version cheapest."
>
  <article class="post">
    <h1>Mario Kart World — Switch 2 Buying Guide</h1>
    <p class="meta">Nintendo Switch 2 · Updated 2026-08-05</p>

    <p>
      <strong>Mario Kart World</strong> is the launch racer for the Nintendo Switch 2
      and the first mainline Mario Kart built for a brand-new console. It leans into
      an open, connected world you can drive across, plus a new <em>Knockout Tour</em>
      eliminat-race format.
    </p>

    <h2>Editions and what you get</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Standard digital</strong> — the full game, always installed on your console</li>
      <li><strong>Bundle with console</strong> — often the first place a discount appears, since retailers cut the bundle even when the standalone stays at list</li>
      <li><strong>Physical cartridge</strong> — resellable, but takes a slot and needs the disc swapped</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Digital vs physical on Switch 2</h2>
    <p>
      As a launch title, Mario Kart World sits at list price for a long time — Nintendo
      first-party games rarely drop early. The smartest saving is usually a
      console bundle rather than waiting for a standalone cut. If you already own the
      console, the digital version is the most convenient way to play immediately.
    </p>

    <h2>Where to buy cheapest</h2>
    <ul class="buy-list">
      <li>
        <AffiliateLink
          network="amazon"
          href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Mario+Kart+World+Switch+2"
          cta="Check on Amazon"
        />
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="note">
      Prices change frequently — always verify on the store before purchasing.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .post { padding: 1.5rem 0; max-width: 720px; }
  .post h1 { font-size: 1.8rem; }
  .meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; }
  .buy-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem; }
  .note { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
</style>
